<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumhuram</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khor Rori</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sumhuram, at Khor Rori on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhofar">Dhofar</a> coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, was a fortified port founded by the Kingdom of Hadramawt in the last centuries BCE to control the frankincense trade. Its inscriptions name it as a royal foundation, and finds of Indian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> pottery show contacts across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. It is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> 'Land of Frankincense'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumhuram.jpg" alt="Sumhuram" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juozas Šalna · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khor_Rori_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
